This Python script implements a PIR occupancy monitoring class using the `gpiozero` library for interfacing with the HC-SR501 PIR motion sensor connected to GPIO 17. The class polls the sensor every 0.5 seconds, applies a debounce interval of 2.0 seconds, and logs each valid detection event with an ISO 8601 timestamp to an internal list. The `get_stats` method returns occupancy statistics, and the `print_summary` method prints a summary report after the polling loop finishes.

The script includes error handling for sensor initialization failures and runtime errors, ensures that resources are cleanly released on all exit paths, and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals gracefully, exiting with code 0 on normal completion or a graceful signal and with code 1 only if initialization fails. The code is designed to work with real hardware as well as with mock backends, avoiding hard-coded driver library dependencies.

